  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-script-element:attr-script-async\r\n\r\n> async — Execute script when available, without blocking\r\n\r\nThis statement is at odds with the diagram:\r\n\r\n![Script Attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/images/asyncdefer.svg \"Script Attributes\")\r\n\r\nThe diagram indicates that the script is loaded _asynchronously_, but is executed _synchronously-.\r\n\r\nThe following paragraph:\r\n\r\n> For classic scripts, if the async attribute is present, then the classic script will be fetched in parallel to parsing and evaluated as soon as it is available (potentially before parsing completes).\r\n\r\nis unclear whether the script is evaluated synchronously or blocks parsing.",
